<title>RUSSIA: Russia launches military, civilian satellites.</title>
<headline>Russia launches military, civilian satellites.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia launched three military and three civilian satellites from the northern Plesetsk cosmodrome on Friday, a military spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said the satellites were launched on schedule at 6.47 a.m. (02.47 GMT).</p>
<p>The spokesman declined to say how the military probes would be used, but he said the three Gonets-1D satellites would help improve communications in some Russian regions.</p>
<p>The first three of these satellites were launched last year and six more will be blasted into orbit by 1998.</p>
</text>
